    category: 'exercise-rehab',
    specialty: 'Physiotherapy',
    bio: 'Lucy is a co-founder and Co-Managing Director of Rehab Physio London, a specialist rehabilitation company delivering expert multidisciplinary therapy across a wide range of complex conditions. She is a neurological physiotherapist with over 20 years of clinical experience, having worked across NHS rehabilitation units and spent several years as a senior clinician in the acute neurological rehabilitation unit at The Wellington Hospital.',
    extendedBio: 'Intensive, multidisciplinary rehabilitation is at the heart of what Lucy does. She has built an in-house team of specialist therapists including occupational therapists, speech and language therapists, neuropsychologists and rehabilitation assistants, who work together to create bespoke programmes around each client\'s individual goals. For Lucy, rehabilitation has always been about more than meeting basic functional needs; it\'s about helping people get back to the life they want to live. The team works primarily in clients\' own homes, providing a discreet and fully tailored service, and Lucy has long been a believer in the power of non-medicalised environments to support recovery. This thinking led her to develop Rehab Escapes, RPL\'s residential rehabilitation intensive in the Cotswolds, where clients benefit from expert therapy alongside the restorative qualities of beautiful countryside and community. Internationally, Lucy and her team have delivered rehabilitation programmes across Central and South America, Switzerland, Africa and the Caribbean, and have worked aboard private yachts in the South of France, supporting clients to keep living their lives whilst continuing their recovery.',
